# Python

## Project structure

- Analysis scripts live in `Python/` (R scripts in `scripts/`). Mirror
  workflows with matching numeric prefixes when both exist.
- Extract reusable logic into modules only when used more than once.
- Keep raw data immutable in `data/raw/`; write processed objects to
  `data/intermediate/`; save figures/tables to `outputs/`.
- Use project-root `pathlib.Path` paths.
- Do not install this repo as a package
  (`[tool.uv] package = false` in `pyproject.toml`).
- Prefer the scverse stack already in use.

## Modern engineering stack

| Tool | Role |
|------|------|
| [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) | Package manager (counterpart of `renv`) |
| [Ruff](https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/) | Lint + format |
| [Pyrefly](https://pyrefly.org/) | Type check |
| [prek](https://github.com/j178/prek) | Git hooks (prefer over pre-commit) |
| [just](https://just.systems/) | Task runner |

- `uv sync` → `just check` (or `uv run ruff` / `pyrefly`) before commit.
- Run scripts with `uv run Python/<script>.py`, not system `python3`.

## Naming and style

- `snake_case` for variables, functions, modules, files.
- `UpperCamelCase` for classes only.
- PEP 8 + modern typing (`list[str]`, `X | None`, `Path`).
- 4-space indent; lines ≤ 88 (Ruff default).
- Type-hint public functions in reusable modules.
- Guard scripts with `if __name__ == "__main__":`.

## Single-cell omics (scverse)

- Central object: `anndata.AnnData`.
- `scanpy` for QC / neighbours / embeddings; `pertpy` for perturbation
  and compositional analyses; `mudata` for multimodal.
- Counts in `.layers["counts"]` or `.raw`; metadata in `.obs` / `.var`.
- Save reusable intermediates as `.h5ad` under `data/intermediate/`.

## Preferred Python dependencies

| Task | Package / tool |
|------|----------------|
| Single-cell core | `scanpy`, `anndata` |
| Perturbation / composition | `pertpy` |
| Fast tabular (non-AnnData) | `polars`, `duckdb` |
| Plotting | `matplotlib`, `seaborn`, `scanpy` |
| Project / env | `uv` |
| Lint / format / types | `ruff`, `pyrefly` |

---

# GitHub Actions (this repo)

- `pkgdown.yaml` — Quarto + pkgdown → `gh-pages` (no network-script step).
- `R-CMD-check.yaml` — Ubuntu release check only for now.
- **No `test-coverage` workflow** until the user requests it.
- CI disables the renv autoloader; installs via `setup-r-dependencies`.
